The interactive viewer (web/) and the shared tile format / meshing pipeline
(scripts/tiles.py, and the structure of several supporting scripts) are adapted
from Piotr Migdał's "Warsaw in voxels" (https://github.com/stared/warsaw-vibe-voxel),
commit 9104d330fd6c8724eb89ccf6ee6d32fa127b7433, MIT License, © 2026 Piotr Migdał.

This Shanghai project does not redistribute Warsaw's generated city tiles or
GUGiK LiDAR / orthophoto derivatives.

Shanghai scene data under web/public/data is derived from:
  - OpenStreetMap, © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL
    https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/
    Extract: https://download.openstreetmap.fr/extracts/asia/china/shanghai.osm.pbf
  - Copernicus GLO-30 DEM (30 m), © European Union, Copernicus Programme
    https://spacedata.copernicus.eu/collections/copernicus-digital-elevation-model

The Oriental Pearl's stepped silhouette is a simplified voxel sculpture from
published dimensions (official / Wikipedia height 468 m, sphere diameters 50 m
and 45 m), not from LiDAR or measured surveys.
